Subject: [PATCH 01813/11362] [outer-loop] energy-prior probes: GGUF (blocked)
 + vLLM (operator path)

GGUF/llama.cpp path dead-ended: GGUF valid (arch=diffusion-gemma) but released
llama-cpp-python 0.3.29 errors 'unknown model architecture: diffusion-gemma' (support is
llama.cpp-master-only). Pivoted to vLLM per operator (native DiffusionGemma support,
vllm.ai/blog/2026-06-10) installed in an ISOLATED venv (~/.cache/vllm-venv) to protect the
conductor from vLLM's strict torch/transformers pins. vLLM probe extracts prompt_logprobs
(= the per-position score, log p(x_i|ctx) ~ -E component); fp8 TP=2 fits 26B on 2x3090.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
